      "doctor_question": "Have you felt this way your entire life, or is this something that started more recently?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Oh, definitely my whole life. It ain't new at all. Like, back when I was a boy in school, my teachers were always moving my seat. I mean constantly. Because I just could not stay put, you know? I was always talking out of turn, and I'd get in big trouble for jumping up before class was even done. I just couldn't wait for that bell. \n\nEspecially in Mrs. Gable's room... she had this huge mole on her chin, right? And every time she talked, it just bobbed up and down. Me and Tommy used to count how many times it moved. Tommy was my best friend back then. He actually got a dirt bike that year, a little Honda. Man, we rode that thing all over the trails behind the old quarry until the chain snapped on us. We tried to fix it with some baling wire, which, let me tell you, do *not* ever try that on a motorcycle. It whipped around and almost took my leg off. You ever ride dirt bikes, Doc? I haven't been on one in years, but I was looking at some on Craigslist last night... people want crazy money for them now, even the beat-up ones.",
